</section>
<section aria-labelledby="example-alert" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="example-alert" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">What an alert says</h2>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Every channel gets the same text. This is the template the alert service sends, filled in with example numbers:</p>
<figure class="m-0 my-4">
<blockquote class="m-0 whitespace-pre-line rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-950/60 dark:text-gray-100">Your Aave Health Factor on Arbitrum is 1.42, which is below your threshold of 1.5. Consider adding collateral or repaying debt to avoid liquidation.

Sent at: Oct 14, 2026, 3:05:00 AM Coordinated Universal Time</blockquote>
<figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Example only: the network, numbers and time are made up. Emails arrive with the subject &quot;Aave Health Factor Alert – Arbitrum&quot;.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="problem" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="problem" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Health factors fall while you sleep</h2>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Aave shows your health factor in its app and warns you inside its transaction screens, but as of October 2026 it doesn&#x27;t send alerts. ETH drops overnight, interest keeps accruing on your debt, or a governance update trims a liquidation threshold, and nothing messages you about any of it.</p>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">On Aave&#x27;s governance forum, one borrower describes<!-- --> <a href="https://governance.aave.com/t/unexpected-or-poorly-executed-settlement-by-the-system/21120" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">checking in the morning to find the position liquidated again</a>; another,<!-- --> <a href="https://governance.aave.com/t/repeatedly-failed-repayment-attempts-leading-to-liquidation/20379" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">an hour of repay transactions that kept failing until the position was liquidated</a>. On the Polygon forum in 2021, before Aave V3, one borrower<!-- --> <a href="https://forum.polygon.technology/t/liquidation-on-polygon-aave-json-error/8067" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">tried to repay at a health factor of 1.01</a> and was liquidated before the transaction went through.</p>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">By the time you look, a liquidator may have taken collateral worth the repaid debt plus a bonus: 5% on WETH in the Ethereum Core market as of October 2026.<!-- --> <a class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200" href="/blog/how-aave-liquidation-works">What happens in an Aave liquidation</a> <!-- -->walks through the rules.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="how-it-works" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="how-it-works" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">How it works, in 4 steps</h2>
<ol class="m-0 grid list-none gap-3 p-0 sm:grid-cols-2">
<li class="m-0 rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<h3 class="m-0 mb-1 text-base font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">1. Connect the wallet you borrow with (read-only, free)</h3>
<p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 dark:text-gray-300">The dashboard shows that wallet&#x27;s Aave V3 collateral, debt and health factor on all 7 networks. Tokenping watches the wallet you connect; you can&#x27;t add another address.</p>
</li>
<li class="m-0 rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<h3 class="m-0 mb-1 text-base font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">2. Unlock alerts: 3 USDC for 30 days, paid on Arbitrum One (approve, then pay)</h3>
<p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 dark:text-gray-300">Two wallet transactions: an approval for exactly the price, never an unlimited one, then the payment. Nothing renews automatically.</p>
</li>
<li class="m-0 rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<h3 class="m-0 mb-1 text-base font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">3. Pick a threshold and your channels for each network (1.1–10, default 1.5)</h3>
<p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 dark:text-gray-300">Each network is a separate alert. Send it to Signal or email, or to more than one.</p>
</li>
<li class="m-0 rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<h3 class="m-0 mb-1 text-base font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">4. We check every 5 minutes and message you while you&#x27;re below it</h3>
<p class="m-0 text-sm leading-relaxed text-base-content/80 dark:text-gray-300">Every check sends one message per channel until your health factor is back at or above your threshold, or you delete the alert. A fast drop can cross 1.0 between two checks.</p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="pricing" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="pricing" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Pricing</h2>
<dl class="m-0 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Dashboard</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 font-semibold text-base-content">Free</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Alerts</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 font-semibold text-base-content">3 USDC per 30 days</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Renewal</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 font-semibold text-base-content">None automatic: you pay again when you want more time</dd>
</div>
<div class="rounded-2xl border border-base-300/80 bg-base-200/60 p-4 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/40">
<dt class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Payment</dt>
<dd class="m-0 mt-1 font-semibold text-base-content">USDC on Arbitrum One, from your wallet (approve, then pay)</dd>
</div>
</dl>
<p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-sm text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">The price is read from the payment contract and refreshed hourly.</p>
<div class="mt-5 flex flex-col items-start gap-2">
<a class="btn btn-primary rounded-full" href="/aave">Set up alerts: 3 USDC for 30 days</a>
<p class="m-0 text-sm text-base-content/70 dark:text-gray-400">Paid in USDC on Arbitrum One. No auto-renew.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="questions" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="questions" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Questions to ask before you connect a wallet</h2>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">Can Tokenping touch my funds?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">No. Tokenping reads your positions and health factor with read-only calls and never asks for an approval or a signature on Aave. The only wallet transactions are the payment for alerts: an approval for exactly the price, never an unlimited one, then the payment, both on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- -->. The payment contract<!-- --> <!-- -->is <a href="https://repo.sourcify.dev/42161/0x79872d7529cfE1c062838fACDA004Ce4BFB16553" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">verified on Sourcify</a> and its<!-- --> <a href="https://github.com/romispectrum/tokenping" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">source code is public on GitHub</a>. It is upgradeable and controlled by the Tokenping team&#x27;s wallet, which can change the price, pause payments, withdraw what was paid and upgrade the contract.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">What do you store?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Your wallet address, the networks and thresholds you set, the channels you picked, and your email address and/or Signal username<!-- -->. If you answer the optional &quot;How did you hear about Tokenping?&quot; question, that answer too. Tokenping keeps no health factor history and no log of sent alerts, and this site runs no analytics. To read your positions, your wallet address is sent to RPC providers. Payments are public on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- -->: anyone can see the paying address, the amount and the new expiry. Until the app checks wallet signatures, anyone who knows your wallet address can look up the contact details saved for it. The<!-- --> <a class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200" href="/privacy">privacy page</a> <!-- -->explains this and lists every service that handles your data.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">What does it cost, and is there a catch?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">The dashboard is free. Alerts cost <!-- -->3 USDC per 30 days<!-- -->, paid in native USDC on <!-- -->Arbitrum One<!-- --> even if your position is on another network, so you need USDC and a little ETH for gas there. It takes two transactions: approve, then pay. Nothing renews automatically, and paying again extends your access from its current end date. The contract has no refund function.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">What if an alert doesn&#x27;t arrive?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Tokenping checks every <!-- -->5<!-- --> minutes. A failed check or message is logged, and the next check tries again while your health factor is still below your threshold. Delivery depends on third parties (Resend for email, a Signal relay,<!-- --> public RPC nodes and Vercel&#x27;s scheduler), and Tokenping is in beta with no uptime guarantee. A fast crash can cross 1.0 between two checks. So pick two channels, set your threshold with room to act, and don&#x27;t make an alert your only safeguard.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">Is my position supported?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Aave V3 on Ethereum (Core market), Polygon, Arbitrum, Optimism, Base, Avalanche and Gnosis. Not supported: Aave V4 (live on Ethereum, Avalanche, Arc and Base as of October 2026), the other Aave V3 markets on Ethereum (Prime/Lido, EtherFi, Horizon), other Aave networks and other protocols. You get one alert per network, for the wallet you connect.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">How often will I be alerted, and how do I stop it?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Every <!-- -->5<!-- --> minutes on each channel you picked, for as long as your health factor is below your threshold. Alerts stop when it is back at or above your threshold, or when you delete the alert, which needs active access. If your access has expired, message us on<!-- --> <a href="https://x.com/tokenping" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">X</a> or in our<!-- --> <a href="https://t.me/tokenping_xyz" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200">Telegram community</a> and we&#x27;ll delete it.<!-- --> There is no snooze, no &quot;recovered&quot; message and no unsubscribe link in the emails yet.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">Can I watch a wallet I don&#x27;t connect, or several wallets?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Not today. Tokenping watches the wallet you connect, and access is per paying wallet.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="m-0 mt-5 mb-1 text-lg font-semibold leading-snug text-base-content">Other tools are free. Why pay?</h3>
<p class="my-2 leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">If a Telegram bot or a mobile app works for you and you&#x27;d rather paste any address than connect a wallet, free tools exist<!-- -->:<!-- --> <a class="link underline-offset-2 text-indigo-700 hover:text-indigo-900 dark:text-indigo-300 dark:hover:text-indigo-200" href="/blog/aave-liquidation-alert-tools">our comparison of Aave liquidation alert tools</a> <!-- -->covers them, including where they beat Tokenping<!-- -->. Tokenping is for people who want the alert on Signal or email, including for positions on Gnosis and Optimism.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="limits" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="limits" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">Limits, stated plainly</h2>
<ul class="m-0 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 marker:text-base-content/50">
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Aave V3 only, on 7 networks, and on Ethereum only the Core market. No Aave V4 and no other protocols.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Checks run every 5 minutes, not in real time. A fast drop can liquidate a position between two checks.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">While you&#x27;re below your threshold, every check sends another message on each channel. There is no snooze, digest or recovery message.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">One threshold per network, for the connected wallet only. No watch-only addresses, price alerts or portfolio-wide alerts.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Payment is in USDC on Arbitrum One only: no card payments, and the contract has no refund function.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Emails have no unsubscribe link yet, and deleting an alert needs active access.</li>
<li class="leading-relaxed text-base-content/90 dark:text-gray-200">Tokenping is in beta. Delivery depends on third-party services, and there is no uptime guarantee.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="from-the-blog" class="rounded-3xl border border-base-300 bg-base-100 p-5 sm:p-6 md:p-8 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60">
<h2 id="from-the-blog" class="m-0 mb-3 text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold leading-tight text-base-content">From the blog</h2>
<ul class="m-0 grid list-none gap-4 p-0">
<li class="m-0 p-0">
<article class="card border border-base-300 bg-base-100 dark:border-white/10 dark:bg-gray-900/60 ">
